## Description

`Application.windowCreated()` (`src/node/desktop/src/main/application.ts`) handles Electron's `did-create-window` event. When a pending satellite/secondary window is found and a window with the same name is already tracked, it raises the existing window and returns early:

```ts
const existingWindow = this.windowTracker.getWindow(pendingWindow.name)?.window;
if (existingWindow) {
  // activate the existing window then deny creation of new window
  raiseAndActivateWindow(existingWindow);
  return;
}
```

By the time `did-create-window` fires, Electron has already created `newWindow`, so the early return does not deny anything. The new window is neither configured, shown, nor destroyed, and it is never registered with the window tracker. Since it keeps the frame name it was opened with, `window-utils.activateWindow(name)` can also match it instead of the intended window.

Outside automation the orphan is visible (Electron shows `window.open()` windows immediately); after #18764 it is created hidden in automation mode, so the leak is invisible there but still present.

## Expected

The early return should either destroy `newWindow` (`newWindow.destroy()`) or the duplicate should be denied earlier, in `windowOpening()`, before Electron creates the window.

Noted during review of #18764.

